This patch is applied to the local ESPHome build input
`openrbus-ble-proxy.yaml`; local secret material must remain in the ignored
`secrets.yaml` file and outside the repository.

1. Add a restored `uint32_t openrbus_read_generation_counter` global,
   initialized to zero. Persistence normally keeps the marker monotonic;
   HA also accepts a changed marker after a reset/reconnect.
2. Add a diagnostic template sensor with id
   `openrbus_read_generation`, update interval `never`, and zero decimal
   places.
3. In `openrbus_extended_response.on_notify`, after publishing the raw
   response, increment the counter and publish it when `openrbus_read_ready`
   is true:

       id(openrbus_read_generation_counter)++;
       id(openrbus_read_generation).publish_state(
         static_cast<float>(id(openrbus_read_generation_counter)));

This marker is the completion/freshness contract for HA. It must be published
for every valid final response, including responses whose raw value is
identical to the previous one.
